msgid "Core types"
msgstr "核心型別"

msgid ""
"Godot has a rich set of classes and templates that compose its core, and "
"everything is built upon them."
msgstr "Godot 具有一套豐富的類別與範本，構成其核心，所有功能皆建立於此之上。"

msgid ""
"This reference will try to list them in order for their better understanding."
msgstr "本參考資料將依序列出這些型別，幫助使用者更好地理解。"

msgid "Allocating memory"
msgstr "記憶體分配"

msgid ""
"Godot has many tricks for ensuring memory safety and tracking memory usage. "
"Because of this, the regular C and C++ library calls should not be used. "
"Instead, a few replacements are provided."
msgstr ""
"Godot 有許多確保記憶體安全和追蹤記憶體使用情況的技巧。因此，不應使用常規的 C "
"和 C++ 庫呼叫。取而代之的是幾個替代方案。"

msgid "For C-style allocation, Godot provides a few macros:"
msgstr "對於 C 風格分配，Godot 提供了一些巨集："

msgid ""
"These are equivalent to the usual ``malloc()``, ``realloc()``, and "
"``free()`` of the C standard library."
msgstr ""
"這些巨集等同於標準 C 函式庫的 ``malloc()``、``realloc()``、``free()`` 功能。"

msgid "For C++-style allocation, special macros are provided:"
msgstr "C++ 風格則提供了特殊巨集："

msgid ""
"These are equivalent to ``new``, ``delete``, ``new[]``, and ``delete[]`` "
"respectively."
msgstr "這些巨集分別對應於 ``new``、``delete``、``new[]`` 與 ``delete[]``。"

msgid ""
"``memnew``/``memdelete`` also use a little C++ magic to automatically call "
"post-init and pre-release functions. For example, this is used to notify "
"Objects right after they are created, and right before they are deleted."
msgstr ""
"``memnew``/``memdelete`` 還利用了一些 C++ 的“魔法”來自動呼叫後初始化（post-"
"init）和預釋放（pre-release）函式。例如，這用於在物件剛建立後以及即將被刪除前"
"通知它們。"

msgid ""
"`core/os/memory.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/os/"
"memory.h>`__"
msgstr ""
"`core/os/memory.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/os/"
"memory.h>`__"

msgid "Containers"
msgstr "容器"

msgid ""
"Godot provides its own set of containers, which means STL containers like "
"``std::string`` and ``std::vector`` are generally not used in the codebase. "
"See :ref:`doc_faq_why_not_stl` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Godot 提供自有的一套容器，表示在程式碼庫中一般不使用 STL 容器，如 "
"``std::string`` 與 ``std::vector``。詳見 :ref:`doc_faq_why_not_stl`。"

msgid ""
"A 📜 icon denotes the type is part of :ref:`Variant <doc_variant_class>`. "
"This means it can be used as a parameter or return value of a method exposed "
"to the scripting API."
msgstr ""
"📜 圖示表示該型別屬於 :ref:`Variant <doc_variant_class>` 的一部分。這代表它可"
"以用於公開給腳本 API 的方法之參數或回傳值。"

msgid "Godot datatype"
msgstr "Godot 資料型別"

msgid "Closest C++ STL datatype"
msgstr "最接近的 C++ STL 資料型別"

msgid "Comment"
msgstr "註解"

msgid "|string| 📜"
msgstr "|string| 📜"

msgid "``std::string``"
msgstr "``std::string``"

msgid ""
"**Use this as the \"default\" string type.** ``String`` uses UTF-32 encoding "
"to simplify processing thanks to its fixed character size."
msgstr ""
"**請作為“預設”字串型別使用。**\\ ``String`` 使用 UTF-32 編碼，字元大小固定，"
"從而簡化了處理過程。"

msgid "|vector|"
msgstr "|vector|"

msgid "``std::vector``"
msgstr "``std::vector``"

msgid ""
"**Use this as the \"default\" vector type.** Uses copy-on-write (COW) "
"semantics. This means it's generally slower but can be copied around almost "
"for free. Use ``LocalVector`` instead where COW isn't needed and performance "
"matters."
msgstr ""
"**將此作為「預設」向量容器使用。** 採用寫入複製（COW）語意，因此一般較慢，但"
"幾乎可以零成本地被複製。若不需要 COW 又重視效能，請改用 ``LocalVector``。"

msgid "|hash_set|"
msgstr "|hash_set|"

msgid "``std::unordered_set``"
msgstr "``std::unordered_set``"

msgid "**Use this as the \"default\" set type.**"
msgstr "**將此作為「預設」集合型別使用。**"

msgid "|a_hash_map|"
msgstr "|a_hash_map|"

msgid "``std::unordered_map``"
msgstr "``std::unordered_map``"

msgid ""
"**Use this as the \"default\" map type.** Does not preserve insertion order. "
"Note that pointers into the map, as well as iterators, are not stable under "
"mutations. If either of these affordances are needed, use ``HashMap`` "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"**將此作為「預設」對映（map）型別使用。** 不保留插入順序。請注意，映射中的指"
"標以及反覆運算器在變異時都不是穩定的。若需要這些特性，請改用 ``HashMap``。"

msgid "|string_name| 📜"
msgstr "|string_name| 📜"

msgid ""
"Uses string interning for fast comparisons. Use this for static strings that "
"are referenced frequently and used in multiple locations in the engine."
msgstr ""
"使用字串駐留以加速比較。適合用在經常被引用、且在引擎多處使用的靜態字串。"

msgid "|char_string|, |char16_string|"
msgstr "|char_string|, |char16_string|"

msgid "``std::u8string`` ``std::u16string``"
msgstr "``std::u8string`` ``std::u16string``"

msgid ""
"``String``-likes that use ``char`` and ``char16_t``, respectively. These are "
"aliases of ``CharStringT<T>``; ``wchar_t`` and others are also supported."
msgstr ""
"``String`` -like 型別分別使用 ``char`` 和 ``char16_t`` ；這些均為 "
"``CharStringT<T>`` 的別名；此外還支援 ``wchar_t`` 等其他型別。"

msgid "|local_vector|"
msgstr "|local_vector|"

msgid ""
"Closer to ``std::vector`` in semantics, doesn't use copy-on-write (COW) thus "
"it's faster than ``Vector``. Prefer it over ``Vector`` when copying it "
"cheaply is not needed."
msgstr ""
"語意更接近 ``std::vector``，不使用 COW，因此比 ``Vector`` 更快。當不需要低成"
"本複製時，優先於 ``Vector`` 使用它。"

msgid "|array| 📜"
msgstr "|array| 📜"

msgid ""
"Values can be of any Variant type. No static typing is imposed. Uses shared "
"reference counting, similar to ``std::shared_ptr``. Uses Vector<Variant> "
"internally."
msgstr ""
"元素可為任意 Variant 型別, 不強制靜態型別。使用共享參考計數, 類似 "
"``std::shared_ptr``. 內部以 Vector<Variant> 實作。"

msgid "|typed_array| 📜"
msgstr "|typed_array| 📜"

msgid ""
"Subclass of ``Array`` but with static typing for its elements. Not to be "
"confused with ``Packed*Array``, which is internally a ``Vector``."
msgstr ""
"``Array`` 的子類別，但其元素具靜態型別。不要與 ``Packed*Array`` 混淆，後者在"
"內部其實是 ``Vector``。"

msgid "|packed_array| 📜"
msgstr "|packed_array| 📜"

msgid ""
"Alias of ``Vector``, e.g. ``PackedColorArray = Vector<Color>``. Only a "
"limited list of packed array types are available (use ``TypedArray`` "
"otherwise)."
msgstr ""
"``Vector`` 的別名，例如 ``PackedColorArray = Vector<Color>``。僅提供有限幾種"
"封包陣列型別（否則請使用 ``TypedArray``）。"

msgid "|list|"
msgstr "|list|"

msgid "``std::list``"
msgstr "``std::list``"

msgid ""
"Linked list type. Generally slower than other array/vector types. Prefer "
"using other types in new code, unless using ``List`` avoids the need for "
"type conversions."
msgstr ""
"連結串列型別。一般比其他陣列/向量型別慢。除非能藉由使用 ``List`` 省去型別轉"
"換，否則在新程式碼中應優先使用其它型別。"

msgid "|fixed_vector|"
msgstr "|fixed_vector|"

msgid "``std::array``"
msgstr "``std::array``"

msgid ""
"Vector with a fixed capacity (more similar to "
"``boost::container::static_vector``). This container type is more efficient "
"than other vector-like types because it makes no heap allocations."
msgstr ""
"具有固定容量的向量（更接近 ``boost::container::static_vector``）。由於不會進"
"行堆積配置，這種容器比其他類向量型別更有效率。"

msgid "|span|"
msgstr "|span|"

msgid "``std::span``"
msgstr "``std::span``"

msgid ""
"Represents read-only access to a contiguous array without needing to copy "
"any data. Note that ``Span`` is designed to be a high performance API: It "
"does not perform parameter correctness checks in the same way you might be "
"used to with other Godot containers. Use with care. ``Span`` can be "
"constructed from most array-like containers (e.g. ``vector.span()``)."
msgstr ""
"用於對連續陣列進行只讀存取，且無需複製任何資料。請注意， ``Span`` 是一款高效"
"能 API：它不採用您在其他 Godot 容器中常見的參數正確性檢查方式；請謹慎使用。 "
"``Span`` 可通過大多數類陣列容器（例如 ``vector.span()`` ）建置。"

msgid "|rb_set|"
msgstr "|rb_set|"

msgid "``std::set``"
msgstr "``std::set``"

msgid ""
"Uses a `red-black tree <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red-black_tree>`__ for "
"faster access."
msgstr ""
"使用 `紅黑樹 <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red-black_tree>`__ 以獲得更快的存"
"取。"

msgid "|v_set|"
msgstr "|v_set|"

msgid "``std::flat_set``"
msgstr "``std::flat_set``"

msgid ""
"Uses copy-on-write (COW) semantics. This means it's generally slower but can "
"be copied around almost for free. The performance benefits of ``VSet`` "
"aren't established, so prefer using other types."
msgstr ""
"使用 COW 語意。因此一般較慢，但幾乎可以零成本地被複製。``VSet`` 的效能優勢尚"
"未明確，建議優先使用其他型別。"

msgid "|hash_map|"
msgstr "|hash_map|"

msgid ""
"Defensive (robust but slow) map type. Preserves insertion order. Pointers to "
"keys and values, as well as iterators, are stable under mutation. Use this "
"map type when either of these affordances are needed. Use ``AHashMap`` "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""
"具防禦性（穩健但較慢）的映射型別。保留插入順序。對鍵與值的指標，以及反覆運算"
"器，在變異下皆是穩定的。當需要其中任一特性時請使用此型別。否則請使用 "
"``AHashMap``。"

msgid "|rb_map|"
msgstr "|rb_map|"

msgid "``std::map``"
msgstr "``std::map``"

msgid ""
"Map type that uses a `red-black tree <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red-"
"black_tree>`__ to find keys. The performance benefits of ``RBMap`` aren't "
"established, so prefer using other types."
msgstr ""
"一種使用 `紅黑樹 <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red-black_tree>`__ 來尋找鍵"
"（key）的 Map 型別。由於 ``RBMap`` 的效能優勢尚未得到證實，因此建議優先使用其"
"他型別。"

msgid "|dictionary| 📜"
msgstr "|dictionary| 📜"

msgid ""
"Keys and values can be of any Variant type. No static typing is imposed. "
"Uses shared reference counting, similar to ``std::shared_ptr``. Preserves "
"insertion order. Uses ``HashMap<Variant>`` internally."
msgstr ""
"鍵與值可為任意 Variant 型別，不強制靜態型別。使用共享參考計數，類似 "
"``std::shared_ptr``。保留插入順序。內部使用 ``HashMap<Variant>``。"

msgid "|typed_dictionary| 📜"
msgstr "|typed_dictionary| 📜"

msgid ""
"Subclass of ``Dictionary`` but with static typing for its keys and values."
msgstr "``Dictionary`` 的子類別，但其鍵與值具靜態型別。"

msgid "|pair|"
msgstr "|pair|"

msgid "``std::pair``"
msgstr "``std::pair``"

msgid ""
"Stores a single pair. See also ``KeyValue`` in the same file, which uses "
"read-only keys."
msgstr ""
"它用來儲存單一的一對資料。另外也可以看看同一個檔案里的 ``KeyValue`` ，不過 "
"KeyValue 里的鍵（key）是只讀的。"

msgid "Relocation safety"
msgstr "重定位安全性"

msgid ""
"Godot's containers assume their elements are `trivially relocatable <https://"
"open-std.org/JTC1/SC22/WG21/docs/papers/2020/p1144r5.html>`__."
msgstr ""
"Godot 的容器（Containers）假設其內部元素是 `trivially relocatable <https://"
"open-std.org/JTC1/SC22/WG21/docs/papers/2020/p1144r5.html>`__。"

msgid ""
"This means that, if you store data types in it that have pointers to "
"themselves, or are otherwise `not trivially relocatable <https://open-"
"std.org/JTC1/SC22/WG21/docs/papers/2020/p1144r5.html#non-trivial-"
"samples>`__, Godot might crash. Note that storing **pointers to** objects "
"that are not trivially relocatable, such as some Object subclasses, is "
"unproblematic and supported."
msgstr ""
"這意味著，如果你在裡面儲存的資料型別包含指向自身的指針，或者由於其他原因導致"
"它不是 `not trivially relocatable <https://open-std.org/JTC1/SC22/WG21/docs/"
"papers/2020/p1144r5.html#non-trivial-samples>`__ ，Godot 可能會崩潰。不過請注"
"意，儲存 **指向** 那些‘非簡單可重定位’物件（比如某些 Object 的子類）的指針，"
"則是完全沒有問題的，並且受到支援。"

msgid ""
"The reason to assume trivial relocatability is that it allows us to make use "
"of important optimization techniques, such as relocation by ``memcpy`` or "
"``realloc``."
msgstr ""
"之所以要假設（某型別）具備平凡可重定位性，是因為這樣我們就能利用一些重要的最"
"佳化技術，比如直接通過 ``memcpy`` 或 ``realloc`` 來進行重定位。"

msgid ""
"`GH-100509 <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100509>`__ tracks "
"this decision."
msgstr ""
"`GH-100509 <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100509>`__ 追蹤此決"
"定。"

msgid "Multithreading / Concurrency"
msgstr "多執行緒 / 併發"

msgid ""
"You can find more information on multithreading strategies "
"at :ref:`doc_using_multiple_threads`."
msgstr ""
"你可以在這裡找到更多關於多執行緒策略的資訊 :ref:`doc_using_multiple_threads`."

msgid ""
"None of Godot's containers are thread-safe. When you expect multiple threads "
"to access them, you must use multithread protections."
msgstr ""
"Godot 的所有容器（Containers）都不是執行緒安全的。如果你預計會有多個執行緒同"
"時存取它們，就必須自行使用多執行緒保護機制。"

msgid ""
"Note that some of the types listed here are also available through the "
"bindings, but the binding types are wrapped with :ref:`class_RefCounted` "
"(found in the ``CoreBind::`` namespace). Prefer the primitives listed here "
"when possible, for efficiency reasons."
msgstr ""
"請注意，這裡列出的某些型別也可以通過綁定（bindings）來使用，但這些綁定型別都"
"被 :ref:`class_RefCounted` (found in the ``CoreBind::`` namespace)包裹了一"
"層。出於效率考慮，請盡可能優先使用這裡列出的原生基礎型別。"

msgid "|mutex|"
msgstr "|mutex|"

msgid "``std::recursive_mutex``"
msgstr "``std::recursive_mutex``"

msgid "Recursive mutex type. Use ``MutexLock lock(mutex)`` to lock it."
msgstr ""
"遞歸互斥鎖（Recursive mutex）型別。請使用 ``MutexLock lock(mutex)`` 語法來對"
"它進行加鎖。"

msgid "|binary_mutex|"
msgstr "|binary_mutex|"

msgid "``std::mutex``"
msgstr "``std::mutex``"

msgid "Non-recursive mutex type. Use ``MutexLock lock(mutex)`` to lock it."
msgstr ""
"非遞歸互斥鎖（Non-recursive mutex）型別。請使用 ``MutexLock lock(mutex)`` 語"
"法來對它進行加鎖。"

msgid "|rw_lock|"
msgstr "|rw_lock|"

msgid "``std::shared_mutex``"
msgstr "``std::shared_mutex``"

msgid ""
"Read-write aware mutex type. Use ``RWLockRead lock(mutex)`` or ``RWLockWrite "
"lock(mutex)`` to lock it."
msgstr ""
"一種能識別“讀/寫”狀態的互斥鎖型別。請使用 ``RWLockRead lock(mutex)`` 或者 "
"``RWLockWrite lock(mutex)`` 的語法來對它進行加鎖。"

msgid "|safe_binary_mutex|"
msgstr "|safe_binary_mutex|"

msgid ""
"Recursive mutex type that can be used with ``ConditionVariable``. Use "
"``MutexLock lock(mutex)`` to lock it."
msgstr ""
"一種可以與 ``ConditionVariable`` 搭配使用的遞歸互斥鎖型別。使用 ``MutexLock "
"lock(mutex)`` 來對它進行加鎖。"

msgid "|condition_variable|"
msgstr "|condition_variable|"

msgid "``std::condition_variable``"
msgstr "``std::condition_variable``"

msgid "Condition variable type, used with ``SafeBinaryMutex``."
msgstr "條件變數型別，需配合 ``SafeBinaryMutex`` 一起使用。"

msgid "|semaphore|"
msgstr "|semaphore|"

msgid "``std::counting_semaphore``"
msgstr "``std::counting_semaphore``"

msgid "Counting semaphore type."
msgstr "計數 semaphore 型別。"

msgid "|safe_numeric|"
msgstr "|safe_numeric|"

msgid "``std::atomic``"
msgstr "``std::atomic``"

msgid "Templated atomic type, designed for numbers."
msgstr "專為數字設計的、基於範本的原子型別。"

msgid "|safe_flag|"
msgstr "|safe_flag|"

msgid "``std::atomic_bool``"
msgstr "``std::atomic_bool``"

msgid "Bool atomic type."
msgstr "布林（Bool）原子型別。"

msgid "|safe_ref_count|"
msgstr "|safe_ref_count|"

msgid ""
"Atomic type designed for reference counting. Will refuse to increment the "
"reference count if it is 0."
msgstr ""
"這是一種專為參照計數設計的原子型別。如果目前的參照計數已經是 0，它將拒絕（或"
"者說無法）再執行遞增操作。"

msgid "Math types"
msgstr "數學型別"

msgid ""
"There are several linear math types available in the ``core/math`` directory:"
msgstr "``core/math`` 目錄中有多種線性數學型別可用："

msgid ""
"`core/math <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/tree/master/core/math>`__"
msgstr ""
"`core/math <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/tree/master/core/math>`__"

msgid "NodePath"
msgstr "NodePath"

msgid ""
"This is a special datatype used for storing paths in a scene tree and "
"referencing them in an optimized manner:"
msgstr "這是一種特殊型別，用於在場景樹中儲存路徑，並以最佳化的方式進行參照："

msgid ""
"`core/string/node_path.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/"
"core/string/node_path.h>`__"
msgstr ""
"`core/string/node_path.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/"
"core/string/node_path.h>`__"

msgid "RID"
msgstr "RID"

msgid ""
"RIDs are *Resource IDs*. Servers use these to reference data stored in them. "
"RIDs are opaque, meaning that the data they reference can't be accessed "
"directly. RIDs are unique, even for different types of referenced data:"
msgstr ""
"RID 是 *Resource ID* (資源識別碼)。伺服器使用這些 ID 來參照其內部儲存的資料。"
"RID 為不透明型別, 無法直接存取其所參照的資料。即使對應的資料型別不同, RID 也"
"保持唯一:"

msgid ""
"`core/templates/rid.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/"
"templates/rid.h>`__"
msgstr ""
"`core/templates/rid.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/"
"templates/rid.h>`__"
